# VTID-03711 — commands actually run.

# Reported live by the platform owner: "Polly TTS speaks for all wired
# languages in Mickey Mouse speed." Investigated in the same session that
# had just dispatched ORB_CASCADED_VOICE_ENABLED=true to production
# (VTID-03703's production follow-up).

# Root-caused by reading the actual code, not guessing:
cat services/gateway/src/orb/live/upstream/cascaded-live-client.ts
#   -> confirmed Polly PCM is synthesized at 16kHz and every chunk is
#      correctly labeled 'audio/pcm;rate=16000' (POLLY_PCM_SAMPLE_RATE_HZ)
grep -n "audio/pcm|rate=|sampleRate|AudioContext" \
  services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js
#   -> found _playAudio(msg.data_b64, msg.mime || 'audio/pcm;rate=24000')
#      at the single WS message dispatch site, and createBuffer(1,
#      floats.length, 24000) hardcoded in _processQueue() — the mime's
#      actual rate was never read.
grep -n "audio/pcm;rate=\${|mime.*rate|sampleRateHz" \
  services/gateway/src/routes/orb-live.ts
#   -> confirmed greeting-bridge and guided-topic-narration audio ALSO
#      send correctly-labeled `mime: audio/pcm;rate=${sampleRateHz}`
#      through the same shared _playAudio() path -- same defect,
#      pre-existing, not introduced by this session.

